{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this admission. Can you tell me what’s been going on with your breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hey, thanks. I’ve been having more trouble breathing, especially at night. I’ve had to wear my humidifier all day and night now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Your dad mentioned your secretions have increased too. Any fever, chills, or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or night sweats. Just more mucus and shortness of breath, like before my last dilation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. We checked your labs and your white blood cell count is high, which suggests inflammation or infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it an infection? I’ve had pseudomonas before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your sputum culture showed Pseudomonas aeruginosa. We’re starting IV antibiotics—cefepime—to treat it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another dilation? I was supposed to have one soon anyway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning a bronchoscopy in the next day or two. Given your symptoms and history, we expect to do another dilation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s what usually helps. What about my prednisone? I’m on 7.5 mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re increasing it to 20 mg daily to reduce airway inflammation. Then we’ll taper it down over a few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my methotrexate? I missed a dose last week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2137-10-05 15:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Rheumatology said it’s okay—you’re on a weekly dose, and the medicine lasts a while. We’ll restart it as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2137-10-06 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your chest X-ray yesterday didn’t show pneumonia, but we’re still concerned about tracheal infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2137-10-06 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the antibiotics are for the trachea, not lungs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2137-10-06 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s called tracheobronchitis. The Pseudomonas is in your airways, causing swelling and more mucus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2137-10-06 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I feel a bit better already with the humidifier and meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2137-10-06 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. We’ll proceed with bronchoscopy tomorrow to clean out secretions and dilate the narrowed areas."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2137-10-07 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, we’re getting ready for your bronchoscopy. They found a new shadow on your left lung this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2137-10-07 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it pneumonia? I thought the X-ray was clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2137-10-07 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, there’s a small area of consolidation. But after your procedure earlier, the follow-up X-ray shows it’s already improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2137-10-07 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well during the bronchoscopy. We dilated your trachea and left main bronchus. There was a lot of inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2137-10-07 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the blockage worse than before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2137-10-07 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The trachea was about 70% narrowed. We opened it up. The left bronchus was completely blocked—we cleared and dilated it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2137-10-07 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds intense. Did you take any samples?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2137-10-07 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we took washings and a small biopsy. Cultures confirmed Pseudomonas, which is sensitive to your current antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2137-10-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat X-ray looks better—no pneumonia now. Lung volumes are still low, but that’s typical for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2137-10-08 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the infection is clearing up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2137-10-08 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and your breathing should keep improving. We’ll keep you on IV cefepime for a few more days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2137-10-08 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I switch to oral antibiotics later?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2137-10-08 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, infectious disease recommends 14 days total. You’ll switch to ciprofloxacin pills before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2137-10-09 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs today show your white count is still high, but that’s expected with inflammation from your condition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2137-10-09 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that normal for me? I remember it was high last time too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2137-10-09 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your history of relapsing polychondritis and ___ syndrome can keep your WBC elevated even without infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2137-10-09 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the NTM my last culture showed? Is that being treated?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2137-10-09 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Infectious disease decided not to treat it now. It’s unclear if it’s active, and we didn’t want to add more antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2137-10-10 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your second bronchoscopy went well. We dilated again and took another biopsy. No new issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2137-10-10 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Do they think the narrowing is getting worse over time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2137-10-10 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It seems the intervals between dilations are shortening, which suggests progression. But your rheumatology team is monitoring that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2137-10-10 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my humidifier? You mentioned something about replacing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2137-10-10 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, because Pseudomonas can live in equipment, we arranged for a new one. Please discard the old humidifier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2137-10-10 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I’ll keep using the tobramycin nebulizer at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2137-10-10 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, twice daily. It helps target Pseudomonas directly in your airways."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you today. You’re breathing comfortably on room air."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds will I be on at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue ciprofloxacin twice daily for one more week, tobramycin nebs twice daily, and the prednisone taper."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the taper is 20 mg, then 15, then 10, then back to 7.5 mg?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll give you clear instructions. Also, follow up with pulmonary and infectious disease soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I start feeling worse again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor or come back if you have fever, increased shortness of breath, or more secretions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, Dr. Lee. I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re glad to see your improvement. The team will get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I avoid sick people?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially with your tracheostomy and immune suppression from prednisone. Try to stay away from crowds and sick contacts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, keep using your albuterol as needed for tightness, and the guaifenesin to help thin mucus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. We’re here to help. You’ll go home with your new humidifier and all your meds sorted."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I’m ready to get back home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2137-10-11 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll have the discharge team finalize everything. Rest up, and take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2137-10-05 15:03:00",
    "admission_end": "2137-10-11 16:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for progressive dyspnea and increased sputum production in the setting of tracheostomy and recurrent tracheobronchial stenosis. He was found to have tracheobronchitis due to Pseudomonas aeruginosa, confirmed by sputum and bronchial cultures. He was treated with IV cefepime, later transitioned to oral ciprofloxacin, and received two bronchoscopies with balloon dilation of the trachea and left main bronchus. His prednisone dose was increased to 20 mg daily to reduce airway inflammation and then tapered. A new humidifier was arranged due to risk of equipment contamination. He improved clinically, maintained oxygenation on room air, and was discharged home with follow-up planned in pulmonary and infectious disease clinics.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute tracheitis with obstruction",
      "Acute respiratory failure with hypoxia",
      "Other specified congenital malformation syndromes, not elsewhere classified",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Relapsing polychondritis",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Pseudomonas (aeruginosa) (mallei) (pseudomallei) as the cause of diseases classified elsewhere"
    ]
  }
}
